# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase connection.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two required values from the
# Supabase dashboard (Project Settings → API).
#
# Both are required. Without them the app renders a "Backend not configured"
# screen instead of starting — there is no offline mode.
#
# These two are meant to be public and ship in the browser bundle. What protects
# the data is the row-level security in supabase/migrations/, not the secrecy of
# these values.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only, and never prefixed VITE_ — Vite inlines every VITE_ variable
# into the browser bundle, and the keys below bypass every row-level security
# policy. They belong in .env.local for the scripts and in the Vercel
# environment for api/, nowhere else.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secret key from Project Settings → API Keys. Used by api/admin-users (creating
# accounts, changing roles, resetting passwords) and by api/keepalive.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Vercel sends this back as the cron Authorization header. Any long random
# string. Without it the keepalive route refuses to run.
# CRON_SECRET=

# Personal access token from https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens.
# Only needed to apply schema migrations with `npm run db:migrate`. It can
# manage every project on the account, so generate it when needed and revoke it
# afterwards.
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
